cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use spanlint or its conformance dataset, please cite it as below.
title: "spanlint: conformance linter for OpenTelemetry GenAI telemetry"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kuciuk
    given-names: Artiom
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24576737
repository-code: https://github.com/inormis/spanlint
url: https://inormis.github.io/spanlint/
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-11-27"
keywords:
  - opentelemetry
  - generative-ai
  - semantic-conventions
  - observability
  - conformance
  - linter
abstract: >-
  spanlint checks whether the telemetry an AI framework emits matches the
  OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions. The repository includes a
  conformance dataset that compares nine AI frameworks across Python, .NET
  and Node against the conventions as of November 2026, with the captured
  OTLP exports, the scripts that produced them and the pinned registry
  commit, so the results can be regenerated.
